<title>UK: IGC cuts 1996/97 China wheat import estimate.</title>
<headline>IGC cuts 1996/97 China wheat import estimate.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Grains Council on Thursday cut its estimate for China's 1996/97 wheat imports to 5.0 million tonnes from a previous estimate of 7.0 million made in November.</p>
<p>In its Grains Market Report the IGC put 1995/96 wheat imports by China at 12.6 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The IGC raised its estimate for Iraq's 1996/97 wheat imports to 1.8 million tonnes from one million in its previous estimate and 0.8 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>In coarse grains, the IGC increased its estimate for Saudi Arabian imports to 5.8 million tonnes, from a previous 5.0 million and 4.2 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>It raised its estimate of South Korea's coarse grain imports to 9.5 million tonnes from a previous 9.0 million, compared with 10.4 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
